%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: graphical rep of data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: What is the primary purpose of graphical representation of data?
    Options:
    - To make reports look attractive
    - To visualize data patterns, trends, and relationships quickly and effectively
    - To replace statistical calculations
    - To hide data limitations
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is most suitable for displaying the frequency distribution
      of a continuous variable?
    Options:
    - Bar Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Pie Chart
    - Histogram
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A bar graph is typically used for representing data that are:'
    Options:
    - Continuous
    - Categorical (Nominal or Ordinal)
    - Skewed
    - Correlated
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: What is the key visual difference between a histogram and a bar
      graph?
    Options:
    - Bar graphs are always vertical
    - Bar graphs are for continuous data
    - Histograms have gaps
    - In a histogram, the bars touch; in a bar graph, they are separated
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A pie chart is most appropriate for showing:'
    Options:
    - The mean and standard deviation
    - The proportion of cases in each category of a categorical variable
    - The correlation between two variables
    - The change in a variable over time
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is best for showing the relationship between two continuous
      variables?
    Options:
    - Histogram
    - Bar Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Pie Chart
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A line graph is most commonly used to display:'
    Options:
    - Categorical proportions
    - The relationship between two categories
    - Frequency distributions
    - Trends over time (Time Series Data)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: A box plot (or box-and-whisker plot) visually displays which of
      the following?
    Options:
    - The correlation coefficient
    - The median, quartiles, range, and potential outliers
    - The regression line
    - The probability distribution
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: In a box plot, the "box" itself represents the range of which percentile
      of the data?
    Options:
    - The middle 50% (Interquartile Range)
    - The bottom 25%
    - The top 25%
    - The entire 100%
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A stem-and-leaf plot is similar to a histogram but has the advantage
      of:'
    Options:
    - Being easier to draw
    - Preserving the original raw data values
    - Showing the mean and standard deviation
    - Being used for categorical data
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is used to display the cumulative frequency of a dataset?
    Options:
    - Scatter Plot
    - Pictogram
    - Bar Chart
    - Ogive (Cumulative Frequency Polygon)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A frequency polygon is created by:'
    Options:
    - Drawing circles
    - Connecting the midpoints of the tops of the bars in a histogram
    - Drawing bars with gaps
    - Plotting individual data points
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which type of chart is most effective for comparing parts of a
      whole?
    Options:
    - Line Graph
    - Bar Graph
    - Pie Chart
    - Scatter Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A graph that uses pictures or symbols to represent data is called
      a:'
    Options:
    - Histogram
    - Pictogram
    - Ogive
    - Stem-and-leaf plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: How does a clustered bar chart differ from a simple bar chart?
    Options:
    - It has no bars
    - It shows trends over time
    - It is always horizontal
    - It compares multiple data series side-by-side for the same categories
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Why is it important to start the y-axis at zero in a bar graph?
    Options:
    - It is not important
    - To avoid misleading visual comparisons of the bar heights
    - To make the graph taller
    - To follow a strict rule
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: A contour plot is a graphical technique for representing a ______-dimensional
      surface.
    Options:
    - One
    - Four
    - Two
    - Three
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: A bubble chart is an extension of which other plot?
    Options:
    - Bar Chart
    - Scatter Plot
    - Line Graph
    - Histogram
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph would you use to track the progress of a project schedule?
    Options:
    - Pie Chart
    - Scatter Plot
    - Gantt Chart
    - Box Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A map that uses color or shading to represent statistical data
      for geographic areas is called a:'
    Options:
    - Scatter Plot
    - Choropleth Map
    - Line Graph
    - Pictogram
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: "Assertion (A):\_Graphical misrepresentation can lead to incorrect
      conclusions.\_Reason (R):\_Manipulating scales, omitting data, or using inappropriate
      graphs can distort the true story of the data."
    Options:
    - Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.
    - Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.
    - A is true but R is false.
    - A is false but R is true.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Contrast a "histogram" and a "bar graph."
    Options:
    - They are identical.
    - 'Histogram: for continuous data, bars touch. Bar graph: for categorical data,
      bars are separated.'
    - 'Histogram: for categories. Bar graph: for continuous data.'
    - Histogram has separated bars.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A researcher wants to show the distribution of exam scores for
      a class of 100 students. The most appropriate graph is a:'
    Options:
    - Pie Chart
    - Line Graph
    - Histogram
    - Scatter Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key advantage of a stem-and-leaf plot
      over a histogram?
    Options:
    - It is more colorful.
    - It can show more than one variable.
    - It is easier for computers to create.
    - It retains the original data values.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A graph that is symmetrical and bell-shaped describes a:'
    Options:
    - Bimodal distribution
    - Normal distribution
    - Positively skewed distribution
    - Uniform distribution
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'In a positively skewed distribution shown on a histogram, the
      tail extends towards the:'
    Options:
    - Left
    - It has no tail
    - Center
    - Right
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "stacked bar chart" is useful for showing:'
    Options:
    - The correlation between variables
    - The total of a category and the sub-groups that compose it
    - The trend over time for one variable
    - The frequency of a single variable
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is most appropriate for displaying the relationship
      between temperature and ice cream sales?
    Options:
    - Histogram
    - Bar Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Pie Chart
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A flaw in a pie chart is that it can be misleading when:'
    Options:
    - It has too few slices
    - It has too many slices, making comparisons difficult
    - It is in color
    - It is used for time series data
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The term "bin" in the context of a histogram refers to the:'
    Options:
    - Y-axis label
    - Data point outside the range
    - Title of the graph
    - Range of values grouped together in a single bar
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "Q-Q Plot" (Quantile-Quantile Plot) is used primarily to check
      if data follows a:'
    Options:
    - Linear trend
    - Theoretical distribution (e.g., Normal distribution)
    - Bimodal pattern
    - Cyclical pattern
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph would best show the percentage of a budget spent on
      different departments?
    Options:
    - Line Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Pie Chart
    - Box Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "violin plot" combines features of a box plot with a:'
    Options:
    - Pie Chart
    - Bar Chart
    - Line Graph
    - Kernel Density Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The primary purpose of a "funnel plot" is to assess:'
    Options:
    - Data distribution
    - Publication bias in meta-analyses
    - Project timelines
    - Correlation strength
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "heatmap" represents data values using:'
    Options:
    - Bar heights
    - Pie slice sizes
    - Line slopes
    - Color intensity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is best for showing the change in a country's population
      over the last 50 years?
    Options:
    - Bar Graph
    - Line Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Histogram
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'In a scatter plot, if the points form a pattern from the lower
      left to the upper right, it indicates a:'
    Options:
    - Positive correlation
    - Negative correlation
    - No correlation
    - Spurious correlation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "radar chart" (or spider chart) is useful for:'
    Options:
    - Showing time series
    - Comparing two means
    - Showing frequency distributions
    - Plotting multivariate data on axes starting from the same point
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The "aspect ratio" of a graph (the ratio of its width to height)
      is important because:'
    Options:
    - It must always be 1:1
    - It can influence the perceived slopes and relationships in the data
    - It determines the color
    - It is only for bar graphs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "Pareto chart" is a combination of a bar graph and a:'
    Options:
    - Pie Chart
    - Box Plot
    - Scatter Plot
    - Line Graph
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The main criticism of 3D effects in graphs (like 3D pie charts)
      is that they:'
    Options:
    - Are more accurate
    - Can distort perception and make data harder to interpret
    - Are easier to create
    - Are required for publication
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A graph that shows the number of observations in each category
      as a series of rectangles is a:'
    Options:
    - Bar Graph
    - Line Graph
    - Scatter Plot
    - Ogive
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which graph is most suitable for identifying outliers in a dataset?
    Options:
    - Pie Chart
    - Line Graph
    - Box Plot
    - Histogram
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "area chart" is essentially a line graph where:'
    Options:
    - The lines are dotted
    - It has no axis
    - The x-axis is categorical
    - The area between the line and the axis is filled with color or shading
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The "legend" in a graph is used to:'
    Options:
    - Make the graph larger
    - Explain the meaning of the symbols, colors, or patterns used
    - Calculate the mean
    - Draw the axis
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "doughnut chart" is a variation of the:'
    Options:
    - Bar Chart
    - Line Graph
    - Pie Chart
    - Scatter Plot
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: Which principle is most important for creating an effective graph?
    Options:
    - Using as many colors as possible
    - Clarity and simplicity (the "data-ink ratio")
    - Making it 3D
    - Using a small font
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "biplot" is a graph that combines:'
    Options:
    - A pie chart and a bar chart
    - A histogram and a box plot
    - Two scatter plots
    - Principal component analysis scores and loadings
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'A "run chart" is a simple plot of data points:'
    Options:
    - In a pie shape
    - In a scatter pattern
    - Over time, with a median line for reference
    - As a 3D surface
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of any graphical representation is to:'
    Options:
    - Be artistically pleasing
    - Communicate the story in the data accurately and efficiently to the viewer
    - Use the latest software
    - Replace all text
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: graphical rep of data
